<title>USA: Mass. housing bonds repriced, top yield 8.26 pct.</title>
<headline>Mass. housing bonds repriced, top yield 8.26 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lehman Brothers said Thursday it repriced Massachusetts Housing Finance Agency's $17.5 million taxable bond issue. The top yield was 8.26 percent in 2020.</p>
<p>The repricing follows:</p>
<p>Massachusetts Housing Finance Agency</p>
<p>RE: $17,460,000*</p>
<p>Insured Rental Housing Bonds, 1996 Series A</p>
<p>(Federally Taxable)</p>
<p>Verbal award.</p>
<p>THE BONDS ARE TAXABLE MUNICIPAL SECURITIES AND THIS OFFERING</p>
<p>IS SUBJECT TO REGULATION BY MUNICIPAL SECURITIES RULE MAKING</p>
<p>BOARD.  ALL ACTIVITY UNDERTAKEN WITH RESPECT TO THIS OFFERING</p>
<p>MUST BE SUPERVISED BY A MUNICIPAL SECURITY PRINCIPAL.</p>
<p>    MOODY'S: Aaa		   S&amp;P: AAA	AMBAC INSURED</p>
<p>    DATED: 11/01/1996	  FIRST COUPON: 07/01/1997</p>
<p>DUE: 07/01</p>
<p>ALL BONDS ARE PRICED AT PAR.</p>
<p>MATURITY		 AMOUNT*    COUPON</p>
<p>07/01/2005		5,080M    7.04  %</p>
<p>					  (Ave life 4.95)</p>
<p>07/01/2010		2,830M    7.79  %</p>
<p>					  (Ave life 11.77)</p>
<p>07/01/2020		9,380M    8.26  %</p>
<p>					  (Ave life 19.53)</p>
<p>				   -------------------------</p>
<p>					TAXABLE INFORMATION</p>
<p> MATURITY	TREASURY   SPREAD VS. TREASURY</p>
<p>		    YIELD</p>
<p>07/01/2005	 6.34	+70</p>
<p>07/01/2010	 6.69     +120</p>
<p>07/01/2020	 6.91     +135</p>
<p>CALL FEATURES: 01/01/2007    102.00</p>
<p>		   DTP 01/01/2009</p>
<p>* - APPROXIMATE SUBJECT TO CHANGE</p>
<p>The award is expected Friday, October 11, 1996.</p>
<p>Delivery is expected on November 14, 1996.</p>
<p>This issue is not book entry.</p>
<p>This issue is pending through DTC.</p>
<p>Lehman Brothers</p>
<p>PaineWebber Incorporated</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
